qvb\"><br \/>\nVariety: 100% Pinot Noir<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"><br \/>\nFermentation: Inox 23-28 C<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"><br \/>\nAging: barrique 225l \u2013 12 months<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"><br \/>\nAlcohol: 14%<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"><br \/>\nSugar: 0.97 g\/l<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"><br \/>\nAcids: 6.30 g\/l<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/p>","description":"<h2><span class=\"HwtZe\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">Method of production: <\/span><\/span><\/span><\/h2>\n<p><span class=\"HwtZe\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">Only grapes from our own are used for production<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"> vineyards located on the territory of the ancient Pannonian Sea.<\/span><\/span> <span class=\"jCAhz\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">Lands<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"> they have a multi-layered composition.<\/span><\/span> <span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">The upper layers are alluvial with several layers of clay and<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"> limestone, the deeper layers are deposits of limestone and fossils from the ancient seabed.<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"> Mandatory careful control of the quality of the berries.<\/span><\/span> <span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">Harvesting is done in the optimum phase<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jCAhz\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\"> ripening.<\/span><\/span> <span class=\"jCAhz ChMk0b\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">Fermentation in stainless steel at a controlled temperature.<\/span><\/span> <span class=\"jCAhz\"><span class=\"ryNqvb\">The wine is closed<\/span><\/span><span class=\"jC